rota lap 5068, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; the row's own discipline is read the actual file and run the actual witness, and running rather than reading is what found both reds this lap
think Opened with the cold endurance run detached and a cadence slice, held the tree still while it ran, and read the card, the claim board and the day shelf meanwhile.
think Cold read 306 guards, 294 green, 12 red, 2 gated, tree_moved=no. One red sat in this lane: vocabulary_collection refused construction/ITINERARY.md on one word of a peer's account line, corpus in reader prose. Swapped to collection; enforce_hits 1 to 0.
think Took petrichor's handoff from the card. claim_preserve is the guard that makes a broad register pass honest, and it refused that ship's settlement/README.md sweep with zero tokens in BEFORE and three in AFTER.
think Ran it rather than trusting the report: CLAIM_PRESERVE_BASE=6e001803b^ over settlement/README.md answers exactly that, and the elder verdict line said only claim tokens drifted.
think The modality half of the same scan split obligation from register one lap earlier and kept its refusal unchanged. Followed that precedent exactly: split the diagnosis, keep the gate, name the door.
obs A dropped token and an added one are one reading until they are counted apart. Only the drop is the fault the guard is named for; an addition under a register pass is still a content change worth seeing, and never a loss.
obs My own first draft counted with grep -c "", which exits 1 on an empty file, so under set -e an unchanged page printed nothing and exited 1. Silence reads like a clean pass. awk END{print NR} answers zero by exiting zero, and leg 1 is the regression guard.
obs The control's first plant moved two tokens rather than one, because the PATH pattern swallows a trailing period. The number sits in its own sentence now, which is a fixture shape a reader can check.
obs Refused to loosen the gate. Whether an addition-only drift may pass is Keaton's word, named on the card rather than taken here.
obs construction/REDS.md closed at 65,533 of the 65,536 it declares. Three bytes. The next red has nowhere to land until a BOOKED row folds, and the row itself was trimmed four times to fit.
obs The pkill trap on the baton fired on me: pkill -f measure_drift.sh matched my own shell's command line and killed the caller, exit 144. tools/f/fleet_call.sh is the bounded form and I used it after.
